WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.977
If you're ready to officially become a seller in the Amazon store, you'll need to list your first

00:00:07.977 --> 00:00:08.420
product.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:12.207
There are a few ways to do this depending on your needs.

00:00:12.207 --> 00:00:17.573
We encourage you to review our guidelines and best practices as well as your options for listing

00:00:17.573 --> 00:00:21.360
as you will likely list products in different ways throughout your journey.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:26.860
First, let's review the two basic types of product listings, existing and new.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:31.660
Existing products are items that are already in the Amazon catalog.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:38.536
When customers shop in the Amazon store, they are able to see all seller offers on a single product

00:00:38.536 --> 00:00:39.260
detail page.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:46.011
This helps customers find the products they want and compare offers and saves you from having to

00:00:46.011 --> 00:00:47.600
recreate product detail pages.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:53.340
When you list an existing product, you'll be adding your offer to an existing page.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:56.235
We refer to this as matching a listing.

00:00:56.235 --> 00:01:00.940
New product listings are items that are not in the Amazon catalog yet.

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:07.155
When listing a new product, you'll need to fill out all the product information in addition to your

00:01:07.155 --> 00:01:07.500
offer.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.473
We refer to this as creating a listing.

00:01:10.473 --> 00:01:16.420
When listing new products, your options depend on the brand that your product is associated with.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:23.561
If a product is part of a brand enrolled in Amazon brand registry, only three types of sellers can

00:01:23.561 --> 00:01:25.440
create its product detail page.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:32.524
The original rights owner who enrolled the brand, other sellers verified as internal to the brand,

00:01:32.524 --> 00:01:35.180
and resellers authorized by the brand.

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:39.780
These are also the only sellers who can match offers on these pages.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:46.665
If a product is part of a brand not enrolled in brand registry, the product owner can create a product

00:01:46.665 --> 00:01:51.140
detail page for it after they secure approval for their unregistered brand name.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:55.260
Other sellers are able to match offers to these pages.

00:01:55.260 --> 00:02:01.094
Finally, if a product is generic, meaning it doesn't have a permanent brand name or logo affixed,

00:02:01.094 --> 00:02:07.271
its product detail page can be created by the product owner using generic as a brand name during

00:02:07.271 --> 00:02:08.300
the listing process.

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:12.340
After the page is created, other sellers can match offers.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:18.682
In some cases, you may be required to complete a selling application for a product or category before

00:02:18.682 --> 00:02:21.500
you can create a new or existing listing.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:26.580
If necessary, you'll be prompted to complete that application during the listing process.

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:32.116
Whether you're matching or creating product listings, there are two ways to list your products,

00:02:32.116 --> 00:02:34.700
one at a time or in bulk.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:38.034
All sellers can list items one at a time.

00:02:38.034 --> 00:02:43.220
That means you'll use a single product ID to match or create a listing.

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:48.700
All sellers can also match or create product variations one at a time.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:55.460
If you have a professional selling plan, you can also match or create listings in bulk using a spreadsheet.

00:02:55.460 --> 00:03:02.148
Step-by-step instructions for listing new or existing products one by one or in bulk can be found

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:06.020
in our guide how to list your products on Seller Central.
